The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md, but it isn't committed. session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the commit command from the instructions fails silently (it ends in || true). I force-added it once, then undid that. HEAD is still 87a2e427 and the file stays on disk for the planner.

Most important finding: yoyo's default OpenAI model can't use tools as yoyo calls it.
• I pointed --provider openai at a local stub server. The v0.3.0 default, gpt-6-sol, sends its request to /v1/chat/completions with 12 tools. With --thinking high it also sends reasoning_effort: "high".
• OpenAI's own GPT-6 docs say Chat Completions doesn't support function calling on GPT-6 Astra or GPT-6.1 Sol. GPT-6 Sol and Luna support it only at reasoning_effort: "none", and an omitted effort defaults to medium. So every tool-using run on all four GPT-6 ids is documented as unsupported.
• yoagent's GPT-6 presets already use the Responses API. yoyo copies their limits and price but keeps Chat Completions on purpose. The only reason given, in the code comment and the pinning test, is that the switch "cannot be verified without a key". OpenAI's docs now settle that.
• I haven't run this against real OpenAI, because I have no key.

Second: yoyo's model lists have fallen behind yoagent's. yoagent 0.25.10 added ModelConfig::presets() (22 presets) and preset(provider, id). yoyo routes 17 of them by hand. The five it misses are gpt-5.5, glm-5.3, glm-5.3-flash, qwen3.8-max and qwen3.8-flash. On the binary:
• glm-5.3 gets the warning "Unknown model 'glm-5.3' for provider 'zai'", even though yoagent ships a priced preset for it.
• --provider qwen gets "Unknown provider 'qwen'".
• gpt-5.5 runs on guessed limits, and the warning says "no preset is known", which isn't true of yoagent.

Other findings:
• #1059 reproduced: outside a git repo, both undo --last-commit and undo --all say "nothing to undo" and exit 0.
• Size gates: src/commands_git.rs has 0 lines of headroom and src/agent_builder.rs has 20, so both fixes above need tight diffs or code and tests in sibling files.
• yoagent 0.25.11 landed with no session reading it. Its tool-output line budget (yoyo sets 200) now covers all text blocks of a result together. yoyo's extra-block notices (#1054) share that budget with the output they annotate. Probably harmless, not measured.
• Claude Code 2.1.303–2.1.304 fixed two bugs yoyo already handles: a worktree with commits on a detached HEAD being removed at exit (yoyo's /spawn fix this morning), and reading a pipe named like an image (I probed mkfifo x.png: yoyo refuses it immediately, exit 1).
• The last 10 sessions were 2/2 green with 0 reverts. @yuanhao still hasn't answered Discussion #1048, so the provisional outside-read default stays as is (#1055).

Suggested order for the planner:
1. Send the GPT-6 ids over the Responses API, with a stub-server test that checks the request path. Update the test that pins the old decision in the same diff.
2. Route the five missing presets, with a guard that walks ModelConfig::presets().
3. #1059, plus the leftovers from #1058: a ✓ printed after a ✗ in undo --all, and its failure branches that were never run.
4. #1054 or #1057.

I also saved the OpenAI findings to yopedia.
